1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to https://archive.org/stream/twohuguenotfamil00foxf/twohuguenotfamil00foxf_djvu.txt, 
2 CONT
2 CONT The de Blois family is issued from the illustrious house of Chatillon
2 CONT by Jean de Blois, son of Jean de Chatillon, comte de Blois (died
2 CONT 1381). One of the grandsons of this Jean de Blois, Guichard de
2 CONT Blois, is the first who seems to have settled in Saintonge by his
2 CONT alliance with Diane de Rabayne from one of the oldest families of
2 CONT this province.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean de Blois, son of Guichard and Diane de Rabayne, married
2 CONT first Isabeau de Fontlebon and second about 1510 Isabeau de
2 CONT Mortagne, lady of Rousillon, the last heiress of this younger branch
2 CONT of the old princes of Mortagne sur Gironde.
2 CONT
2 CONT By reason of this alliance the chatellenie of Rousillon became
2 CONT the name of this branch of the de Blois family settled in Saintonge.
2 CONT
2 CONT My Ancestor, and ancestor of Gregoire de Blois, an ancestor of all the thousands of French Canadians today with surnames Gregoire or de Blois.
