1 NAME Johann /von Kleve/ I
2 GIVN Johann
2 SURN von Kleve
2 NSFX I
1 NAME Johann I, Graf von Kleve
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1293
2 PLAC Cleves, Germany
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 MAY 1368
1 OCCU Graf von Kleve
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} —-
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_%28Kleve%29 (translated) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann von Kleve (* around 1292/93; † 19. November 1368) was from 1347 to 1368 Graf von Kleve.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann was the second son from the second marriage of Count Dietrich VI./VIII. of Kleve with Margareta von Neu-Kyburg. Since he had initially embarked on a spiritual career, he married only late, in 1348, Mechtild von Geldern, the
2 CONC  sister of Duke Rainald III of Geldern, with whom he had no descendants. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann was the father of several illegitimate children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT
2 CONT As a younger son, Johann initially had no prospect of a succession in the county of Kleve. At the latest in 1310 he had embarked on a spiritual career and was a canon in Cologne, Mainz, Trier, Utrecht and Xanten; from 1320 to 1347
2 CONC  he was dean at Cologne Cathedral. In 1318 he made a consolidation with his brother Count Dietrich IX. von Kleve, through which Johann also became Lord of Linn. Around 1333 there was a dispute between the two Kleve brothers about 
2 CONC the succession in the county, since Count Dietrich had three daughters but no son. From 1338, Dietrich obviously accepted the future succession of his brother. In the last years of Count Dietrich's life, Johann was able to gain gr
2 CONC eat influence on his policy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann took over the rule in Kleve after the sonless death of his brother Dietrich on the 7th. July 1347 and renounced his spiritual dignity. Through a marriage with Mechtild von Geldern, Johann was drawn into the Geldrian fratern
2 CONC al war between Duke Rainald III of Geldern and his brother Eduard, whereby the Kluver Count supported the side of Rainald and the Hekeren. Although this commitment brought Kleve the profit of the city of Emmerich, it plunged the c
2 CONC ounty into financial difficulties. Count Johann is considered an important modernizer of the Kleve territory, who in particular expanded the count's chancery into a powerful authority (registered since about 1360).
2 CONT
2 CONT Succession
2 CONT
2 CONT With Johann's death in 1368, the old Klever Grafenhaus died out. Several applicants competed for succession in Kleve. Johann's great-nephew Adolf von der Mark, the brother of Count Engelbert III von der Mark, was finally able to a
2 CONC ssert; the competitors Dietrich von Horn and Otto von Arkel were unsuccessful. The House of Mark ruled Kleve until 1609.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Genealogy 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANCONIA%20(LOWER%20RHINE).htm#DietrichVIKlevedied1305
2 CONT
2 CONT DIETRICH [VI] von Kleve, son of DIETRICH [V] Graf von Kleve & his wife Aleidis von Heinsberg [Sponheim] ([1256/57]-4 Oct 1305).  … m secondly (Erfurt 14 Jul 1290) MARGARETA von Habsburg, daughter of EBERHARD von Habsburg Graf von 
2 CONC Kiburg & his wife Anna von Kiburg (-10 Apr [1333]).  Dietrich [VI] & his second wife had seven children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.         JOHANN (-9 Dec 1368).  "Th. comes Cliuensis" granted "oppido Duseborgensi…domine Margarete matri nostre" as dowry to "Nese sorori nostre…et…Adolpho comiti de Monte cum eadem sorore nostra" by charter dated 31 Mar 1312, 
2 CONC in the presence of "matri nostre…et Johannis ac Euerardi fratrum nostrorum"[2209]. … m (before 22 Feb 1348, Papal dispensation 28 May 1350) as her second husband, MECHTILD van Gelre, widow of GODEFROI Comte de Looz-Chiny, daughter
2 CONC  of REINALD [II] Graaf van Gelre & his first wife Sophie Berthout Vrouwe van Mechelen ([1325]-Huissen 21 Sep 1384, bur Arnhem).  …
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HOLLAND.htm#MechteldGeldernM2JohannIIKleve
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         MECHTILD ([1325]-Huissen 21 Sep 1384, bur Mariendael near Arnhem). …  m firstly (Nov 1336) GOTTFRIED von Heinsberg Comte de Looz et de Chiny, son of DIETRICH Herr von Heinsberg Comte de Looz et de Chiny & his wife Kunig
2 CONC unde von der Mark ([1320/21?]-killed [Prussia/eastern Baltic or Algeciras?] [8 Aug 1342?] [before 16 Oct 1342, bur Mechelen Franciscans]).  m secondly (before 22 Feb 1348, Papal dispensation 28 May 1350) JOHANN II Graf von Kleve, 
2 CONC son of DIETRICH [VI] Graf von Kleve & his second wife Margareta von Habsburg (-9 Nov 1368).  m thirdly (14 Feb 1372) JEAN de Châtillon Comte de Blois et de Dunois, son of LOUIS [I] de Châtillon Comte de Blois & his wife Jeanne de 
2 CONC Beaumont [Hainaut] (-Jun 1381). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Literature
2 CONT * https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_%28Kleve%29 Cites 
