1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Marie of Guelders (died 12 May 1405) was one of two pretenders to the title of Duchess of Guelders and Countess of Zutphen on behalf of her son during the War of the Guelderian Succession from 1371 to 1379.
2 CONT The war began after the deaths of her brothers''', Reginald III of Guelders and Edward of Guelders. Edward died from wounds received at the Battle of Baesweiler, and Reginald, who was known as the fat, died months later. '''Succes
2 CONC sion was also claimed by Marie's sister''', Mathilda, whose side was called the Heeckerens and were led by Frederik van Heeckeren van der Eze (1320-1386). '''Her party was called the Bronckhorsters and was led by Gijsbert V van Br
2 CONC onckhorst (1328-1356). Upon victory of her party, the title of Duke of Guelders went to her son''', William.[1]
2 CONT '''Marie was daughter of''' Reginald II, Duke of Guelders and Sophie Berthout, lady of Malines. '''On 25 December 1362 she married William II, Duke of Jülich († 1393). They had three children:'''[1]
2 CONT *William (1364 † 1402), duke of Guelders (as William I) and of Jülich (as William VII)
2 CONT *Reinald († 1423), duke of Guelders (as Reinald IV) and of Jülich
2 CONT *Joanna, who married John V, Lord of Arkel († 1428)
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria,_Duchess_of_Guelders
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Mary (Joan) of Guelders'''1
2 CONT Last Edited	4 Apr 2020
2 CONT F, #17904, '''d. 12 May 1405'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	Rainald II Rufus, Duke of Guelders, Count Zutphen b. c 1295, d. 12 Mar 1343
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Sophie de Berthout d. 6 May 1329
2 CONT Charts	Pedigree of James Irvine
2 CONT '''     Mary (Joan) of Guelders married Wilhelm VI, Duke of Julich''', son of Wilhelm I, Marquis & Duke of Juliers, Prince of the Empire, Earl Cambridge and Jeanne (Johanna) of Hainault. '''Mary (Joan) of Guelders died on 12 May 1
2 CONC 405'''.
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT '''Wilhelm VI, Duke of Julich''' d. 13 Dec 1393
2 CONT '''Children	'''
2 CONT *Wilhelm III (VIII), Duke of Geldern, Graf von Zutphen+2 b. 31 Mar 1363, d. 16 Feb 1402
2 CONT *Johanna von Julich+ b. c 1364
2 CONT *Reinald IV, Graf von Geldern, Zutphen, & Julich2 b. c 1365, d. 25 Jun 1423
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S5244] Unknown author, Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles by Paget, p. 196.
2 CONT 2.[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. VI, Tafel 33.
2 CONT From: https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p596.htm#i17904
2 CONT ________
2 CONT '''Marie van Gelre'''1 
2 CONT F, #107239, '''d. 12 May 1405'''
2 CONT Last Edited=2 Jun 2013
2 CONT '''     Marie van Gelre was the daughter of''' Reinoud II 'de Zwarte' Hertog van Gelre Graaf van Zutphen and Sophie Berthout Vrouwe van Mechelen.1 '''She married Wilhelm II Herzog von Jülich''', son of Wilhelm I Herzog von Jülich 
2 CONC and Jeanne d'Avesnes, '''in 1362.1,2 She died on 12 May 1405'''.
2 CONT '''Children of Marie van Gelre and Wilhelm II Herzog von Jülich'''
2 CONT 1. Johanna von Jülich+2 b. 1363, d. 19 Jul 1415
2 CONT 2. Wilhelm III Herzog von Jülich Hertog van Gelre b. 6 Mar 1364, d. 16 Feb 1402
2 CONT 3. Reinoud III Herzog von Jülich Hertog van Gelre+ b. 1365, d. 1423
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 91. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT 2.[S3268] Hans Harmsen, "re: Chester Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 21 August 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Chester Family."
2 CONT From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p10724.htm#i107239
2 CONT ___________
2 CONT Maria wife of Willem II of Gulik and the mother of the seven year old heir of that Dukedom Willem III, for whom she was the regents and for whom she claimed Gelre.
2 CONT
2 CONT While in 1377  Emperor Charles IV handed the fief of Gelre to William III of Gulik the power struggle continued. Both fractions had their own powerbrokers and war lords, but eventually it was still Maria who won that battle and in
2 CONC  1379 claimed the throne for her son Willem III of Gulik (1364 – 1402). http://paulbuddehistory.com/europe/gelre/
2 CONT _________________
