2 CONT Marguerite de Valois (1295-1342)
2 CONT
2 CONT Un article de Wikipédia, l'encyclopédie libre.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marguerite_de_Valois_(1295-1342)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite de Valois (1295-1342) est la troisième fille de Charles de France, comte de Valois et de sa première femme Marguerite d'Anjou.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elle épouse en 1310 Guy Ier de Châtillon, comte de Blois, dont elle aura trois enfants:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Louis Ier († 1346), comte de Blois, de Dunois et de Fréteval
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Charles de Blois (1319 † 1364), duc de Bretagne,
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Marie (1323 † 1363) qui en 1334 épouse en premières noces Raoul, duc de Lorraine puis en secondes noces Fréderic Comte de Linanges (Leiningen).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy I, Count of Blois
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Guy I of Blois-Châtillon)
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy I of Blois-Châtillon (died August 12, 1342), son of Hugh II of Châtillon and Beatrix of Dampierre, was count of Blois and lord of Avesnes 1307–1342.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1310, he married Marguerite of Valois, daughter of Charles of Valois and sister of Philip VI of France. They had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis I of Châtillon (d. 1346)
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles of Blois (d. 1364)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie, married in 1334 Rudolph, Duke of Lorraine (d. 1346), married secondly Frederick VII, Count of Leiningen-Dagsburg.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_of_Valois,_Countess_of_Blois
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Valois (1295–1342) was a French noblewoman. She was a daughter of Charles, Count of Valois and his first wife Margaret, Countess of Anjou and thus a sister of King Philip VI of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1310, she married Guy I, Count of Blois. They had three children together:
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis I of Châtillon (d. 1346) Charles of Blois (d. 1364) Marie, married: in 1334 to Rudolph, Duke of Lorraine (d. 1346) Frederick VII, Count of Leiningen-Dagsburg.
2 CONT
