1 NOTE {geni:about_me} After his first wife  Irmgard died childless in 1283 a year after her father had died, Reinoud claimed the duchy. This claim was recognized by King Rudolph I of Germany. This led to the battle of Woeringen in 1288 
2 CONC where the Duke of Brabant defeated the Count of Gelre and his allies (See Duchy of Brabant). Limburg – that since recently had come under the control of Gelre – became now part of Brabant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reinoud second wife was Margaretha a daughter of  Gwijde de Dampierre, Count of Flanders. Two of her sisters were married to the other regional powers Jan II of Brabant and Jan I of Holland. To make it super confusing, Guy de Damp
2 CONC ierre was married twice, and used the same names for the children of both marriages, so Reinoud’s mother was named Margaretha, like her older half-sister who was the mother of Jan II of Brabant.
2 CONT
2 CONT The younger Margaretha was first married on 14 November 1282 to the Lord Alexander, heir to the throne of Scotland and nephew of Edward I, but he died in January 1284, and on 3 July 1286 she married Reinoud I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Because of the large personal debts Reinoud had run up during the war against Brabant – in particular by private investors, – interestingly these included several Lombards in Brabant as well as the Knight Templar in Flanders and i
2 CONC n Paris – his father-in-law Count Gwijde  became his  beneficiary, however in exchange he also became the Regent of Gelre, during which period – 1289- 1293 – Gelre’s administration was modernised and reformed. This also led,  in p
2 CONC articular under Reinoud II, to financial arrangements with the the cities in Gelre, initially for guarantees from Jews and Lombards, but increasingly also for lending. In exchange cities often achieved tax and toll advantages and/
2 CONC or received income from domains or other processions of the count. Withe the Gelre  cities as guarantors the count was also active on foreign financial markets in Brabant and in North Germany, selling annuities in exchange for cre
2 CONC dits. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://paulbuddehistory.com/europe/gelre/
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ARMSTRONG HOME PAGE:Information about Marguerite de Dampierre
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marguerite de DampierreMarguerite de Dampierre (b. 1265, d. 1331) Marguerite de Dampierre (daughter of Guy de Dampierre and Isabelle de Luxembourg) was born 1265 in Dampierre, Jura, France, and died 1331.She married (1) Rainald V
2 CONC an Gelre.She married (2) Alexander II Armstrong on 15 Nov 1282 in Roxburgh, Roxburghshire, Scotland559, son of Bruce Armstrong. Notes for Marguerite de Dampierre: Individual RecordFamilySearch™ Pedigree Resource File  Marguerite d
2 CONC e DampierreCompact Disc #125Pin #858088(AFN: 9FTW-8V) Sex: F Birth:abt 1265  Place:, Dampierre, Jura, France Death:1331Place: Unknown Father:Guy de DampierreDisc #125Pin #858090 Mother:Isabelle de LuxembourgDisc #125Pin #858078  M
2 CONC arriage(s):  Spouse:Rainald Van GelreDisc #125Pin #867882  Marriage:3 Jul 1286Place:, Zutphen, Gelderland, Netherlands Spouse:Alexander ArmstrongDisc #125Pin #854364  Marriage:15 Nov 1282  Place: Roxburgh, Roxburghshire, Scotland 
2 CONC Submitter:  Maitland Dirk BROWER  158 West 600 North Salt Lake City, Utah 84103 More About Marguerite de Dampierre: Date born 2: 1265, Jedburgh, Roxburghshire, Scotland.559 Died 2: 1331, Flandre, Belgium.559 More About Marguerite 
2 CONC de Dampierre and Alexander II Armstrong: Marriage: 15 Nov 1282, Roxburgh, Roxburghshire, Scotland.559 Children of Marguerite de Dampierre and Alexander II Armstrong are: +Alexander III Armstrong, b. 1320, Mangerton Castle, Dumphri
2 CONC eshire, Scotland 559, 559, d. 1398, Hermitage Castle, Lindores, Fifeshire, Scotland 559, 559.
