1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''William II, Duke of Jülich (c. 1327 – 13 December 1393) was the second Duke of Jülich and the sixth William in the House of Jülich. He was the second son''' of William I of Jülich and Joanna of Hainaut.[1]
2 CONT '''William was co-ruler from 1343. He quarreled greatly with his father and imprisoned him from 1349-1351. He tried for many years in Holland-Zeeland to enforce claims against the House of Wittelsbach but failed. When his father d
2 CONC ied in 1361, William became the second Duke of Jülich, his elder brother Gerhard having predeceased their father. He led the traditional feuds of the House of Jülich and lost Kaiserswerth and Zülpich, among others. William interve
2 CONC ned in favor of Edward in the catastrophic war of succession between his brothers-in-law Reinald and Edward for control of the Duchy of Guelders. He took part in the 1371 Battle of Baesweiler (in which Edward was mortally wounded)
2 CONC  and captured Wenceslaus I, Duke of Luxembourg.[2] His brother-in-law Reinald died later in 1371 and as neither Reinald nor Edward left heirs, another fight for the succession of Guelders arose between William and his wife Maria (
2 CONC sister to Reinald and Edward) and Maria's sister Mathilde, wife of John II, Count of Blois. In 1377, Emperor Charles IV granted Guelders to William's son William, but the title was not secured until 1379. Among other territories, 
2 CONC William acquired Monschau-Montjoie, Randerath and Linnich.'''
2 CONT Family and children
2 CONT '''William married in December 1362 to Maria of Guelders''' (c. 1328 – November 1397), daughter of Reinald II of Guelders.[3] '''They had three children''':
2 CONT 1. William (1364–1402)[3]
2 CONT 2. Reinald (c. 1365 – 1423)[3]
2 CONT 3. Joanna, married John V, Lord of Arkel.[3] She succeeded her brother Reinald as Duke of Guelders and was the grandmother of Arnold, Duke of Guelders
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_II,_Duke_of_J%C3%BClich
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Wilhelm VI, Duke of Julich'''1
2 CONT Last Edited	4 Apr 2020
2 CONT M, #17903, '''d. 13 December 1393'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	Wilhelm I, Marquis & Duke of Juliers, Prince of the Empire, Earl Cambridge b. c 1299, d. 26 Feb 1361
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Jeanne (Johanna) of Hainault b. c 1315, d. 1374
2 CONT Charts	Pedigree of James Irvine
2 CONT '''     Wilhelm VI, Duke of Julich married Mary (Joan) of Guelders''', daughter of Rainald II Rufus, Duke of Guelders, Count Zutphen and Sophie de Berthout. '''Wilhelm VI, Duke of Julich died on 13 December 1393.'''
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT '''Mary (Joan) of Guelders''' d. 12 May 1405
2 CONT '''Children	'''
2 CONT *Wilhelm III (VIII), Duke of Geldern, Graf von Zutphen+ b. 31 Mar 1363, d. 16 Feb 1402
2 CONT *Johanna von Julich+ b. c 1364
2 CONT *Reinald IV, Graf von Geldern, Zutphen, & Julich b. c 1365, d. 25 Jun 1423
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S5244] Unknown author, Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles by Paget, p. 196.
2 CONT From: https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p596.htm#i17903
2 CONT ___________
2 CONT '''Wilhelm II Herzog von Jülich'''1 
2 CONT M, #4704, '''b. 1330, d. 13 December 1393'''
2 CONT Last Edited=2 Jun 2013
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.78%
2 CONT '''     Wilhelm II Herzog von Jülich was born in 1330.1 He was the son of''' Wilhelm I Herzog von Jülich and Jeanne d'Avesnes. '''He married Marie van Gelre''', daughter of Reinoud II 'de Zwarte' Hertog van Gelre Graaf van Zutphen
2 CONC  and Sophie Berthout Vrouwe van Mechelen, '''in 1362.2,1 He died on 13 December 1393'''.
2 CONT '''     He gained the title of Herzog von Berg. He gained the title of Herzog von Kleve. He gained the title of Herzog von Jülich. On 15 June 1366 he surrendered his father's English Earldom to King Edward III.'''3
2 CONT '''Children of Wilhelm II Herzog von Jülich and Marie van Gelre'''
2 CONT 1. Johanna von Jülich+1 b. 1363, d. 19 Jul 1415
2 CONT 2. Wilhelm III Herzog von Jülich Hertog van Gelre b. 6 Mar 1364, d. 16 Feb 1402
2 CONT 3. Reinoud III Herzog von Jülich Hertog van Gelre+ b. 1365, d. 1423
