1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John I, Marquis of Namur
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT John's second wife was Marie of Artois (1291 – January 22, 1365, Wijnendaele), Lady of Merode, daughter of Philip of Artois and Blanche of Brittany. They were married by contract in Paris on 6 March 1310, confirmed Poissy, January
2 CONC  1313. John granted her as dower the castle of Wijnendale in Flanders, ratified by the Count of Flanders (his half-brother, Robert III) in 1313.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT John of Namur 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marquis of Namur 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1310/12 - 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 April 1335 
2 CONT
2 CONT Succeeded his father in 1330 as John II, Marquis of Namur. Buried at Kloster Spaltheim.
2 CONT
