2 CONT
2 CONT 12 March 1336 
2 CONT
2 CONT Succeeded his brother in 1335 as Guy II, Marquis of Namur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry of Namur 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1312/13 – 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 October 1333 
2 CONT
2 CONT Canon at Chartres Cathedral; canon at Cambrai Cathedral, 1324; canon at Chalons-sur-Marne and Reims, 1325.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche of Namur 
2 CONT
2 CONT Queen consort of Sweden and Norway 
2 CONT
2 CONT ? - 
2 CONT
2 CONT autumn 1363 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was accused by the noblewoman Birgitta Birgersdatter (Saint Bridget of Sweden) of having poisoned the latter's son, her innocence of the crime only being proved at the end of the 18th century. She lived at Tønsberghus castle i
2 CONC n Norway from 1358, because of the political situation in Sweden, and administered the fiefs of Vestfold and Skienssysla. Married 5 November 1335 at Bohus Castle Magnus IV of Sweden. He was deposed in 1344 as King of Norway, and i
2 CONC n 1363 as King of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip of Namur 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marquis of Namur	
2 CONT
2 CONT 1319 - 
2 CONT
2 CONT September 1337	
2 CONT
2 CONT Succeeded his brother in 1336 as Philip III, Marquis of Namur. Murdered at Famagusta.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Namur 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gräfin von Vianden 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dame de Pierrepont	
2 CONT
2 CONT 1322 - 
2 CONT
2 CONT before 29 October 1357	
2 CONT
2 CONT Married firstly, in 1335/36, Henry II, Graf of Vianden, son of Philip II, Graf of Vianden and his first wife Lucia von der Neuerburg. Her first husband was murdered at Famagusta in September 1337. Married secondly (1340, dispensat
2 CONC ion 9 September 1342) her father's second cousin, Theobald of Bar, Seigneur de Pierrepont, son of Erard of Bar, Seigneur de Pierrepont et d'Ancerville (himself son of Theobald II of Bar), and his wife Isabelle of Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Namur 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1323 -13 September 1383	
2 CONT
2 CONT A nun at Peteghem.
2 CONT
2 CONT William of Namur 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marquis of Namur	
2 CONT
2 CONT 1324 -1 October 1391	
2 CONT
2 CONT Succeeded his brother in 1337 as William I "the Rich", Marquis of Namur. Buried at the Franciscan convent in Namur. Father of William II, Marquis of Namur, and John III, Marquis of Namur, who sold Namur to Philip the Good.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert of Namur 
2 CONT
2 CONT Seigneur de Beaufort-sur-Meuse et de Renaix	
2 CONT
2 CONT 1325 -1/29 April 1391	
2 CONT
2 CONT Seigneur de Beaufort-sur-Meuse et de Renaix; Marshal of Brabant. Married firstly (dispensation 18 October 1354) Isabelle of Hainault, sister of Philippa of Hainault, daughter of William III, Count of Hainault and his wife Joan of 
2 CONC Valois. Married secondly (4 February 1380) as her first husband, Isabeau de Melun, heiress of Viane, daughter of Hugues de Melun, Seigneur d'Antoing (-1409). Robert had two illegitimate children by unknown mistresses.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis of Namur 
2 CONT
2 CONT Seigneur de Peteghem et de Bailleul	
2 CONT
2 CONT 1325 -1378/86	
2 CONT
2 CONT Seigneur de Peteghem et de Bailleul. Flemish counsellor. Governor of Namur 1351. Married on 17 May 1365 Isabelle de Roucy, Dame de Roucy, daughter and heiress of Robert II, Count of Roucy and his wife Marie d'Enghien (-after 1396)
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth of Namur 
2 CONT
2 CONT Electress Palatine	
2 CONT
2 CONT 1329 -29 March 1382	
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Rupert I, Elector Palatine, in autumn 1350 or summer 1358. Died without children in Heidelberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche was married in Paris sometime after November 1281 to Philip of Artois, who was the son of Robert II of Artois and Amice de Courtenay. The couple had seven children, they were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (1285–1311), married in 1301 Louis, Count of Évreux
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert III of Artois (1287–1342), married in 1318 Joan of Valois
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella (1288–1344), a nun at Poissy
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan (1289 – aft. 1350), married in 1301 in Senlis, Gaston I, Count of Foix
2 CONT
2 CONT Othon (died 2 November 1291)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie (1291 – January 22, 1365, Wijnendaele), Lady of Merode, married in 1309 in Paris John I, Marquis of Namur. She was the mother of Blanche of Namur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine (1296–1368, Normandy), married John II of Ponthieu, Count of Aumale
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie av Artois tillhörde den mäktiga kapetingiska ätten Artois, nära släkt med det franska kungahuset.
