1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LOTHARINGIAN%20(LOWER)%20NOBILITY.htm#HeinrichIVSalmdied1292
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHANN [II] & PHILIPPA van Valkenburg  had children: 
2 CONT # SIMON [II] von Salm (c1360-16 Jan 1397).  Graf von Salm.  
2 CONT
2 CONT # MARGARETA von Salm (c1360 -1428).  
2 CONT
2 CONT # JOHANN [III] von Salm (c1360-killed in battle Bulgneville 2 Jul 1431).  Graf von Salm.  
2 CONT
2 CONT *Married firstly (20 Mar 1403)
2 CONT
2 CONT GUILLEMETTE de Vergy, daughter of GUILLAUME de Vergy & his wife Elisabeth von Rappoltstein.  
2 CONT
2 CONT *Married secondly (1429) as her second husband
2 CONT
2 CONT JEANNE de Joinville, widow of HENRI d´Ogeviller, daughter of ANSEAU de Joinville Seigneur de Bonney & his wife --- (-after 1431). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Bulgn%C3%A9ville
2 CONT
2 CONT The Battle of Bulgnéville fought on 2 July 1431 . The battle was fought between two cousins René I d'Anjou and Antoine de Vaudémont over partition of the Duchy of Lorraine after the death of Duke Charles II. Although René was defe
2 CONC ated and captured, the result was reversed by diplomatic means in the years following.
