1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==John V, Lord of Arkel==
2 CONT '''John V, Lord of Arkel (11 September 1362 in Gorinchem – 25 August 1428 in Leerdam) was Lord of Arkel, Haastrecht and Hagestein and stadtholder of Holland, Zeeland and West Frisia. He was a son''' of Lord Otto of Arkel and his w
2 CONC ife, Elisabeth of Bar-Pierrepont.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He acquired the Lordship of Haastrecht in 1380 and Hagestein in 1382. When he inherited Arkel from his father in 1396, he became a member of the court council of the Count of Holland.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During the reign of Albert I, the county suffered from a series of conflicts known as the Hook and Cod wars. John V sided with Albert I and the Cods. However, during a campaign in West Frisia, John V came into conflict with Alb
2 CONC ert's son, William VI, who sided with the Hooks. The murder of Aleid van Poelgeest may also have played a role in their animosity. Albert informed his father that John was no longer a faithful ally and John declared himself indepe
2 CONC ndent and refused to participate in further campaigns against the Frisians. This triggered the Arkel War, in which William VI conquered Arkel. John V lost his land and spent the years 1415-1426 in captivity.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John V died in Leerdam in 1428. His son''' William inherited his claim on the Land of Arkel.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 18 October 1376, John married Joanna of Jülich''', a daughter of Duke William II of Jülich and heiress to the Duchy of Guelders. She died in 1394. '''John and Joanna had two children:
2 CONT *William (d. 1 December 1417 in Gorinchem)
2 CONT *Maria (d. 1415, in IJsselstein), married John II, Count of Egmond
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John had several illegitimate children:
2 CONT *Otto (d. 1475, in Utrecht)
2 CONT *Hennekeyn
2 CONT *Henneke, married John of Egmond, Lord of Wateringen
2 CONT *Dirk
2 CONT
2 CONT William died when he tried to reconquer Gorinchem, which had been a possession of Arkel for many years. He was between 30 and 34 years old and had no male heir. The Land of Arkel was divided between Holland and Guelders.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_V,_Lord_of_Arkel
2 CONT ___________
2 CONT *'''Johann XII, Lord of Archlen, Hagestein, Pierrepont, & Ameide1
2 CONT *'''M, #17901, b. 1363, d. 25 August 1428
2 CONT *Father	Otto, Herr von Arkel b. c 1330, d. 26 Mar 1396
2 CONT *Mother	Elizabeth (Isabel) de Bar b. c 1345, d. b 11 May 1411
2 CONT *'''     Johann XII, Lord of Archlen, Hagestein, Pierrepont, & Ameide was born in 1363 at of Leerdam, Zeeland, Netherlands. A contract for the marriage of Johann XII, Lord of Archlen, Hagestein, Pierrepont, & Ameide and Johanna vo
2 CONC n Julich was signed on 18 October 1376. Johann XII, Lord of Archlen, Hagestein, Pierrepont, & Ameide died on 25 August 1428 at Leerdam, Zeeland, Netherlands; Age 65.
2 CONT *'''Family     Johanna von Julich''' b. c 1364
2 CONT *'''Child	
2 CONT **Maria von Arkel+ b. c 1389, d. 18 Jul 1415
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S5242] Unknown author, Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles by Paget, p. 196; Europaische Stammtafeln by Isenburg, chart 168, Vol. 5.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p596.htm#i17901 
2 CONT _______________
2 CONT *'''Johan VII Heer van Arkel Heer van Pierrepont en Hagestein1
2 CONT *'''M, #4699, b. 1362, d. 25 August 1428
2 CONT *Last Edited=5 Oct 2013
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.01%
2 CONT *'''     Johan VII Heer van Arkel Heer van Pierrepont en Hagestein was born in 1362 at Leerdum, The Netherlands.1 He was the son''' of Otto Heer van Arkel and Elisabeth de Bar-Mousson, Dame de Pierrepont. '''He married Johanna von
2 CONC  Jülich''', daughter of Wilhelm II Herzog von Jülich and Marie van Gelre, '''on 18 October 1376.1 He died on 25 August 1428.
2 CONT *'''Child of Johan VII Heer van Arkel Heer van Pierrepont en Hagestein and Johanna von Jülich
2 CONT **Maria van Arkel-Pierrepont+ b. 1389, d. 19 Jul 1415
