2 CONT
2 CONT At the age of twenty-five he ascended to the throne. Indecisive, and dominated by the policies of his father, he followed the dictates of others, first of Pierre de la Broce and then of his uncle Charles I of Anjou, king of Naples
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1285, the last year of his reign, Philippe made an unsuccessful attempt to annex the kingdom of Aragon. In the aftermath of this struggle, while retreating from Girona, Philippe III died. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip III, King of France, was born April 3, 1245, died Oct. 5, 1285. 
2 CONT
