2 TITL Phillip III King of France
2 NOTE Philip III (30 April 1245 – 5 October 1285), called the Bold (French: le Hardi), was the King of France, succeeding his father, Louis IX, and reigning from 1270 to 1285. He was a member of the House of Capet.
3 CONT
3 CONT Read more about Phillip III in his profile.
