1 NOTE Philip III (of France), called The Bold (1245-85), king of France 
2 CONT (1270-85), the son of King Louis IX, born in Poissy, near Paris. A weak 
2 CONT ruler, he was dominated at various times by his chamberlain, his wife, his 
2 CONT mother, and especially his uncle Charles I of Anjou, king of the Two 
2 CONT Sicilies. In 1285, the last year of his reign, Philip made an unsuccessful 
2 CONT attempt to annex the kingdom of Aragón.
