1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_of_Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick of Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT 	This article does not cite any references or sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unsourced material may be challenged and removed. (November 2007)
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick of Lorraine (1371 – October 25, 1415 in the battle of Agincourt) was Count of Vaudemont.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Duke John I of Lorraine and younger brother of Charles II. In 1393, Frederick married Margaret the heiress of Vaudemont and Joinville, and became Count of these lands in her right. He founded the House of Vaudemo
2 CONC nt, a junior branch of the Duchy of Lorraine.
2 CONT
2 CONT His children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Antoine, who succeeded as Count of Vaudemont,
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Isabelle, who married Philipp I of Nassau-Weilburg, and
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Margaret, who married Thibault II of Blamont.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dynastic problems in the senior side made his great-grandson René of Vaudemont Duke of Lorraine in 1473.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] See also
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Dukes of Lorraine family tree
2 CONT
2 CONT Stub icon 	This biographical article of a European noble is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it.
2 CONT
2 CONT This page was last modified on 22 December 2009 at 16:43.
2 CONT
