1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Blanche of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Blanche de Dreux)
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche of Brittany (1271-1327) was a daughter of John II, Duke of Brittany and his wife Beatrice of England. She is also known as Blanche de Dreux.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche was married to Philip of Artois, who was the son of Robert II of Artois. The couple had six children, they were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite (1285–1311), married in 1301 Louis, Count of Évreux
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert III of Artois (1287–1342)
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle (1288–1344), a nun at Poissy
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne (1289 – aft. 1347), married in 1301 in Senlis Gaston I, Count of Foix
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie (1291 – January 22, 1365, Wijnendaele), Lady of Merode, married in 1309 in Paris John I, Marquis of Namur
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine (1296–1368, Normandy), married John II of Ponthieu, Count of Aumale
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche's husband served under his father at the Battle of Furnes, where he was wounded. He never recovered, and died of the effects over a year later. His premature death led to a legal battle later, when Artois was left to his s
2 CONC ister Mahaut rather than his son Robert. Robert was never the proper Count of Artois, on Mahaut's death Artois passed to her daughter, Jeanne II, Countess of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche's daughter, Marguerite was the mother of Philip III of Navarre who was married to Joan II of Navarre. Her sister, Marie was married to Guy IV, Count of Saint-Pol.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche died on 19 March 1327 at the Chateau de Bois-de-Vincennes, and was buried at the Église des Jacobins in Paris. http://www.montjoye.net/chateau-de-vincennes
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
