1 NOTE She was the heiress of the Countship of Holland and governed Holland and Sealand from 1256 to 1263.
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Aleida was probably about sixteen when she married Jan d'Avesnes, the future Count of Hainault, and they had seven children. However their marriage lasted only eleven years as her husband died in 1257. From 1258 until 1263 she was
2 CONC  regent in Holland for her nephew, Count Floris V. She founded the city of Schiedam, and in 1275, she gave it city rights. She died between 1 March and 9 April 1284 and was buried in Valenciennes.
