2 CONC is IX of France. His mother was Beatrice of Burgundy, heiress of Bourbon and grandaughter of Hugh IV, Duke of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought on the losing side in both the Battle of the Golden Spurs (1302) and the Battle of Mons-en-Pévèle (1304), but escaped unharmed. In 1310, he was made Grand Chamberlain of France. In 1327, Charles IV of France persuaded hi
2 CONC m to exchange the County of Clermont for that of La Marche, and elevated Bourbon to a duchy-peerage. However, Clermont was restored to him by Philip VI of France in 1331.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1310, Louis married Mary of Avesnes, daughter of John II of Avesnes, Count of Hainaut and Holland. They had eight children.
