1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY Son of Wolfert I van Borselen, Lord of Vere and Zandenburg and Sibilie Praet. On 11 May 1309 Wolfert and his brothers were paid compensation for the murder of their father. On 8 April 1312, the pope gave Wolfert dispensa
2 CONC tion to marry Aleid, an ille gitimate daughter of a relative, the Count of Holland, as they were related within the prohibited degree. Wolfert and Aleid had a son and a daughter. Wolfert died before 6 April 1317, and his widow mar
2 CONC ried Otto, Lord of Buren. She died after 12 Jun e 1351.
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT Son of Wolfert I van Borselen, Lord of Vere and Zandenburg and Sibilie Praet. On 11 May 1309 Wolfert and his brothers were paid compensation for the murder of their father. On 8 April 1312, the pope gave Wolfert dispensation to ma
2 CONC rry Aleid, an illegitimate daughter of a relative, the Count of Holland, as they were related within the prohibited degree. Wolfert and Aleid had a son and a daughter. Wolfert died before 6 April 1317, and his widow married Otto, 
2 CONC Lord of Buren. She died after 12 June 1351.
