1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Herpert van Foreest. (1472-1501)
2 CONT Belgian politician
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Herpert van Foreest (mentioned 1472 – The Hague , 1501 ), Lord of the Manor of the Rhineland Lordship of Middelburg and of Schoterbosch , Sheriff of Alkmaar , Alderman , Mayor and Member of the Council of Delft , and Castellan of 
2 CONC Woerden .
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Herpert van Foreest was born as the son of Willem van Foreest and Adriana Hart van der Woert. In 1473 , he succeeded his father in his manorial lordships in Rijnland and Schoterbosch. In 1474, he acquired the lordship belonging to
2 CONC  the House of "Egmond" in Heiloo , and in 1475 the lordship belonging to the House of "Naaldwijk" in Warmond . In 1477, he married Maria van Cats, a descendant of a prominent Zeeland family. Maria van Cats was the daughter of Wolf
2 CONC ert van Cats ( 1410–1467 ) and NN van Sabbingen .
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1480 to 1483 , Herpert van Foreest was an alderman of Delft , and in 1482 he was mentioned as a member of the city council and the Council of Forty. Afterwards, he moved to Alkmaar and became sheriff there in 1484 and 1485. I
2 CONC n this capacity, Herpert was charged with commanding the city's militias and fought alongside his uncle Jan van Foreest (1451-1501) and other Hollanders on the side of Bishop David of Burgundy in the Utrecht War. Subsequently, he 
2 CONC returned to Delft . In 1485 , 1487 , and 1488 , he was an alderman , and in 1490 he was appointed mayor of Delft . Additionally, he was bailiff of Woerden from 1491 to 1495 , and held the associated positions of dike warden , cast
2 CONC ellan, and steward .
2 CONT
2 CONT Herpert drew up his will in 1499. This shows that he was residing in The Hague at the time , where he presumably owned a house on the Westeinde. He also owned a house in Abbenbroek , which he bequeathed to his widow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Because Herpert had no sons but did have daughters, the ancestral Rhineland manorial estates were lost from the family. Two daughters were born from his marriage to Maria van Cats:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ursula van Foreest ( Wijk aan Zee , ca. 1479 - Gouda , May 15, 1525 ), buried in St. John's Church in Gouda . She married ca. 1499 with Jacob van Borselen ( Gouda , 1471 - Gouda, December 20 , 1521 ). He was a son of Jacob van Bor
2 CONC selen ( 1437–1503 ) and Agnes van Raephorst .
2 CONT Anna van Foreest ( 1485 - 1540 ), buried in IJsselstein
2 CONT ''''''
2 CONT Sources, notes and/or references
2 CONT Foreest, HA van (1950): The Old Van Foreest Family , Van Gorcum & Comp. NV, Assen
2 CONT Cox, JCM (2005): De Heeren van Alkmaer; Regeerders en regenten, vroedschap en raad 1264-2005 , Gemeente Alkmaar, Alkmaar, ISBN 90-73131-06-5
