2 CONT Joan, Countess of Ponthieu
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT Jump to navigationJump to search
2 CONT Joan
2 CONT Queen consort of Castile and León
2 CONT Tenure	1237–1252
2 CONT Countess of Ponthieu
2 CONT Reign	1251–1279
2 CONT Predecessor	Marie
2 CONT Successor	Eleanor
2 CONT Countess of Aumale
2 CONT Reign	1239–1279
2 CONT Predecessor	Simon
2 CONT Successor	John I
2 CONT Born	1220
2 CONT Died	16 March 1279 (aged 58–59)
2 CONT Abbeville, France
2 CONT Spouse	Ferdinand III of Castile
2 CONT Jean de Nesle, Seigneur de Falvy et de La Hérelle
2 CONT Issue
