2 CONT Jeanne de Dammartin
2 CONT Birth:  1220
2 CONT Death:  Mar. 16, 1279, France
2 CONT
2 CONT French Nobility. Countess of Ponthieu and Aumale in her own right and queen consort of Castile and Leon by marriage. Born the eldest daughter of Simon de Dammartin and Marie de Ponthieu. She married Ferdinand III of Castile in 123
2 CONC 5 and bore him five children, including Eleonore, later Queen of England. She succeeded her father as Countess of Aumale in 1239 and her mother as Countess of Ponthieu and Montreuil in 1251. After Ferdinand's death, she quarreled 
2 CONC with her stepson Alfonso X of Castile over the lands and income she should have received as a dowager queen. Due to her strained relations with Alfonso, she returned to Ponthieu where she married Jean de Nesle in 1261.
2 CONT
