1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00014204&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT William II of Dampierre
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT William II (1196 – 3 September 1231) was the lord of Dampierre from 1216 until his death. He was the son of Guy II, constable of Champagne, and Matilda, heiress of Bourbon.
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother, Archambaud VIII, inherited Bourbon and he Dampierre. He married Margaret II, Countess of Flanders and Hainault, in 1223 and was thus regent of Flanders until his death as "Willem (or Guillaume) I."
2 CONT
2 CONT He had four children (three sons) by Margaret and the eldest took part in the War of the Succession of Flanders and Hainault:
2 CONT
2 CONT William III, Count of Flanders and Lord of Kortrijk
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy, Count of Flanders and Margrave of Namur
2 CONT
2 CONT John I, Lord of Dampierre, Viscount of Troyes, and Constable of Champagne
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna, married in 1239 to Hugh III of Rethel, then in 1243 to Thiebaut II of Bar
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.dutchgenealogy.nl/was-eleanor-of-aquitaine-my-ancestor-generation-25-guy-of-dampierre/
