2 CONT Although he managed to expand his kingdom, the adverse effect was converting most of the old banates into semi-independent and violently anti-Hungarian principalities. The predominant religion of the area was Greek-Orthodox, and f
2 CONC orceful proselytization to Catholicism provoked rebellion[dubious – discuss][citation needed]. Natural dynastic competition with the Orthodox Serbian and Bulgarian tsars and the emergence of a new Wallachia also contributed to the
2 CONC  uprising.
