2 CONT Charles Robert died at Visegrád, Hungary[1] in 1342.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages and children First marriage Charles married three times.[5] His first wife was Maria of Bytom, a member of the Piast dynasty.[6] She was a daughter of Casimir of Bytom and his wife Helena.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles and Maria possibly had two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Katharine of Hungary, married Henry II of Świdnica and was mother of Anne of Świdnica; Anna was the third wife of Charles IV, Holy Roman Emperor and mother of Wenceslaus, King of the Romans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth Anjou of Hungary (d.1367), married Boleslaw of Opole. Some believe that Katherine and Elisabeth were daughters of Elisabeth of Poland, Charles's third wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Second marriage In 1318, Charles married his second wife Beatrix of Luxembourg. She was a daughter of Henry VII, Holy Roman Emperor and Margaret of Brabant. Beatrix was a younger sister of both John of Bohemia and Marie de Luxembo
2 CONC urg, Queen of France. In November 1319, Beatrix died after giving birth to a stillborn child.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Third marriage On 6 July 1320, Charles married his third wife Elisabeth of Poland. She was a daughter of Władysław I the Elbow-high and Hedwig of Kalisz.[8] Her maternal grandparents were Boleslaus of Greater Poland and Jolenta of
2 CONC  Hungary. They had five sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles (1321).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ladislaus (Belgrade, 1 November 1324 – 24 February 1329).
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis I of Hungary (1326–1382).
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew, Duke of Calabria (1327–1345).
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen, Duke of Slavonia (1332–1354).
