1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elizabeth of Sicily, duchess consort of Bavaria=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Frederick II-III de Aragón, king of Sicily and Eleanor of Anjou, queen consort of Sicily 
2 CONT * Elisabeth of Sicily (1309–1349) was a daughter of Frederick III of Sicily and Eleanor of Anjou. Her siblings included: Peter II of Sicily and Manfred of Athens. After her death her title was given to Georgia Lanza.
2 CONT * Two of their sons became Duke of Bavaria and their daughter, Agnes became Queen of Cyprus by her marriage to James I of Cyprus. Her granddaughter and namesake was Isabeau of Bavaria, queen of France by her marriage to Charles VI
2 CONC  of France. Isabeau's children included: Isabella, Queen of England; Catherine, also queen of England; Michelle, duchess of Burgundy and Charles VII of France.
2 CONT * Elisabeth died in 1349, her husband later married Margarete of Nuremberg; they had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Family and Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married two times. First, 27 June 1328 with Elizabetta of Sicily, daughter of King Frederick III of Sicily and Eleanor of Anjou. Second, he married 14 February 1359 with Margarete of Nuremberg, daughter of John II of Nuremb
2 CONC erg and Elisabeth of Henneberg. All his children were from first marriage, including three sons, who finally divided Bavaria among themselves in 1392 and one daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Stephen III of Bavaria-Ingolstadt''' (1337–September 26, 1413, Niederschönfeld).
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Frederick of Bavaria-Landshut''' (1339–December 4, 1393,Budweis).
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''John II of Bavaria-Munich''' (1341–1397).
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Agnes''' (b. 1338), married c. 1356 King James I of Cyprus.
2 CONT
