1 NOTE Jeanne de Bourbon, Queen of Charles V of France died in 1878 in childbirth.  She was age 41.  She was the mother of eight children, survived by her husband, two sons, and the newborn child.  The others, especially one of her five 
2 CONC daughters died shortly after her mother.
1 NOTE Jeanne de Bourbon (Vincennes, February 3, 1338 – February 6, 1378, Paris) was the Queen of France, due to her marriage to King Charles V. Jeanne was the daughter of Peter I, Duke of Bourbon and Isabelle de Valois, a half-sister of
2 CONC  Philip VI of France as the daughter of Charles of Valois and his third wife Mahaut of Chatillon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father, grandfather, and brother were all somewhat mentally unstable, and Jeanne seems to have inherited this family ailment. She suffered a complete nervous breakdown after the birth of her seventh child. Her eldest surviving
