2 CONC  Montpellier, son of Pedro II 'the Catholic', King of Aragon, Marquis of Carlat, Count of Gerona, Barcelona, Osona, Bésalu, Cerdagne, & Roussillon, Seigneur de Montpellier and Marie of Montpellier, on 8 September 1235 at Barcelona
2 CONC , Catalonia, Spain; They had 5 sons (Pedro, King of Aragon & Sicily; Jaime, King of Majorca, Count of Roussillon & Cerdagne; Fernando; Sancho; & Sancho, Archbishop of Toledo) &.2,3,4,5,6 Violante (Yolante) of Hungary died on 12 Oc
2 CONC tober 1251 at Huesca, Aragon, Spain; Buried at Valbona.6 Family Jaime I 'the Conqueror', King of Aragon, Majorca, & Valencia, Count of Barcelona, Urgel, Gerona, Osona, Bésalu, Cerdagne, & Roussillon, Seigneur de Montpellier b. 12 
