2 NOTE Isabella of France (c. 1295 – August 22, 1358), known as the She-Wolf of France, was the Queen consort of Edward II of England and mother of Edward III. She was the youngest surviving child and only surviving daughter of Philip IV
3 CONC  of France and Joan I of Navarre.
3 CONT
3 CONT Isabella was born in Paris on an uncertain date, probably between May and November 1295, to King Philip IV of France and Queen Jeanne of Navarre.
3 CONT
3 CONT Read more about Isabelle in her profile.
