1 NOTE Ruled France 1316-1322. [GADD.GED]
1 NOTE He was called The Tall.  He became regent for his infant nephew John, king 
2 CONT of France, and after the death of John proclaimed himself king. In 1320, 
2 CONT at the conclusion of the war against Flanders begun during the reign of 
2 CONT Philip IV, France acquired some Flemish territory. Philip frequently 
2 CONT convoked the Estates-General. He made administrative reforms and attempted 
2 CONT to unify coinage, weights, and measures but encountered strong opposition 
2 CONT in the Estates-General. He imposed heavy fines on Jews. Philip died 
2 CONT without a male heir.
