1 NOTE He was also, as Charles I, king of Navarre (1322-28). Called Charles the 
2 CONT Fair.  In 1327 Charles helped his sister Isabella to dethrone her husband, 
2 CONT King Edward II of England. During his reign Charles increased taxation, 
2 CONT exacted burdensome duties, debased the coinage, and confiscated estates. 
2 CONT He died without a male heir, thus ending the direct line of the Capetian 
2 CONT dynasty.
1 NOTE OR "KARL"; KNOWN AS "CHARLES THE FAIR"; HOLY ROMAN EMPORER; KING OF BOHEMIA;
2 CONT KING OF FRANCE 1322-1328 (ACCEDED 1/3/1322, CRWONED AT RHEIMS 2/21/1322)
1 NOTE King of France, the third son of Philip the Fair, ascended in 1322 the French throne, after the death of his brother, Philip V. With him the direct line of the Capets became extinct. [The Home University Encyclopedia, 1946]
