2 NOTE In this illustration is Alice Perrers by the bed side of Edward III.
3 CONT
3 CONT Alice Perrers (1348 – 1400/1401) was a royal mistress whose lover and patron was King Edward III of England. She met him originally in her capacity as a lady-in-waiting to Edward's consort, Philippa of Hainault. As a result of her
3 CONC  liaison, she acquired significant land holdings. She also outlived Phillippa by some 26 years. 
