1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert II de Bourgogne
2 CONT
2 CONT http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roberto_II_de_Borgo%C3%B1a
2 CONT
2 CONT Se casó en 1279 con la princesa Inés de Francia, hija de Luis IX el Santo y Margarita de Provenza. De esta unión nacieron:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Juan (1279 - 1283);
2 CONT * Margarita (1285 - muerta joven);
2 CONT * Blanca (1288 - 1348), casada en 1307 con el conde Eduardo de Saboya;
2 CONT * Margarita (1290 - 1315), casada en 1305 con el futuro rey de Francia y rey de Navarra Luis X el Obstinado;
2 CONT * Juana (1293 - 1348), casada en 1313 con el también futuro rey de Francia Felipe VI de Valois;
2 CONT * Hugo (1294 - 1315), duque de Borgoña, con el nombre de Hugo V;
2 CONT * Eudes (1295 - 1349), duque de Borgoña, con el nombre de Eudes IV;
2 CONT * Luis (1297 - 1316), rey titular de Tesalónica;
2 CONT * María (1298 - ¿?), casada en 1310 con el duque Eduardo I de Bar;
2 CONT * Roberto (1302 - 1334), conde de Tonnerre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roberto II murió el 21 de marzo de 1306 en Vernon-sur-Seine, y fue enterrado en Citeaux.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II, Duke of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II of Burgundy (1248 – March 21, 1306) was duke of Burgundy between 1271 and 1306. Robert was the third son of duke Hugh IV and Yolande of Dreux. Robert married princess Agnes of France, youngest daughter of king Louis IX i
2 CONC n 1279 and had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh V, Duke of Burgundy (1282–1315)
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche (1288–1348), married Edward of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite (1290- 1315), married king Louis X of France
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan (Jeanne) (ca.1290–1348), married count of Maine and Valois, king Philip VI of France
2 CONT
2 CONT Eudes IV, Duke of Burgundy (1295–1350)
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis, King of Thessalonica (1297–1316), married Matilda of Hainaut
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (1298–1336) married Edward I of Bar
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, count of Tonnerre (1302–1334), married Joanna, heiress of Tonnerre
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert ended the practice of giving away parts of the Burgundian estate to younger sons and as dowries to the daughters. From then on, the whole duchy, however already diminished by earlier dowries, passed unfragmented to the elde
2 CONC st son.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_II,_Duke_of_Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II, Duke of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II of Burgundy (1248 – 21 March 1306) was duke of Burgundy between 1271 and 1306, inheriting the title from his brother Eudes of Burgundy, who had no male heirs. Robert was the third son of duke Hugh IV and Yolande of Dreux
2 CONC . Robert married princess Agnes of France, youngest daughter of king Louis IX in 1279[1] and had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hugh V, Duke of Burgundy (1282–1315)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Blanche (1288–1348), married Edward of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Margaret (1290–1315), married king Louis X of France
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Joan (1293–1348), married count of Maine and Valois, king Philip VI of France
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Eudes IV, Duke of Burgundy (1295–1350)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Louis, King of Thessalonica (1297–1316), married Matilda of Hainaut
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Mary (1298–1336) married Edward I of Bar
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Robert, count of Tonnerre (1302–1334), married Joanna, heiress of Tonnerre
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert ended the practice of giving away parts of the Burgundian estate to younger sons and as dowries to the daughters. From then on, the whole duchy, however already diminished by earlier dowries, passed unfragmented to the elde
2 CONC st son.
2 CONT
