1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marie de Bourgogne1
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #102060, b. circa 1290
2 CONT
2 CONT      Marie de Bourgogne was born circa 1290.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She was the daughter of Robert II de Bourgogne, Duc de Bourgogne and Agnes de France.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 She married Edouard I de Bar, Comte de Bar, son of Henry III de Bar, Comte de Bar and Eleanor of England, in 1310.
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p10206.htm#i102060
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert II, Duke of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married princess Agnes of France, youngest daughter of king Louis IX in 1279 and had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh V, Duke of Burgundy (1282–1315)
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche (1288–1348), married Edward of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite (1290- 1315), married king Louis X of France
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan (Jeanne) (1293-1348), married count of Maine and Valois, king Philip VI of France
2 CONT
2 CONT Eudes IV, Duke of Burgundy (1295–1350)
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis, King of Thessalonica (1297–1316), married Matilda of Hainaut
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (1298–1336) married Edward I of Bar
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, count of Tonnerre (1302–1334), married Joanna, heiress of Tonnerre
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward I of Bar
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1310, he married Mary, daughter of Robert II, Duke of Burgundy. By his wife, he left three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry IV, his successor
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor (died 1332), married (1330) Rudolph, Duke of Lorraine, son of Frederick IV
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice, married Guy I of Gonzaga, Lord of Mantua
