1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marie Valois
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Valois (September 18, 1344, Saint-Germain-en-Laye - October 15, 1404) was the sixth child and second daughter of John II of France and Bonne of Bohemia.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a younger sister of (among others) Charles V of France, Louis I of Naples, John, Duke of Berry and Philip II, Duke of Burgundy. She was also an older sister of Agnès of Valois.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1364, Marie married Robert I, Duke of Bar. They were parents to eleven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles of Bar (d. 1392).
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri of Bar (d. September 25, 1396). Killed at the Battle of Nicopolis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippe of Bar (d. September 25, 1396). Killed at the Battle of Nicopolis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward III, Duke of Bar (d. October 25, 1415). Killed at the Battle of Agincourt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean of Bar (d. October 25, 1415). Killed at the Battle of Agincourt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis, Duke of Bar (d. 1431). Bishop of Verdun and bishop of Chalon, later a Cardinal. He was childless and his designated heir and eventual successor was René I of Naples.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Bar. Married William II, Marquis of Namur in 1384.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yolande of Bar. Married John I of Aragon in 1384.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bonne of Bar. Married Waleran III of Luxembourg, Count of Ligny in 1393.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna of Bar (d. January 15, 1402). Married Theodore II, Marquess of Montferrat in 1393.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yolande the Younger of Bar. Named after older sister for uncertain reasons. Married Adolf, Duke of Jülich and Berg.
