1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Blanca de La Cerda y Lara
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanca Fernanda de la Cerda y Lara (c. 1317 – 1347) was a Spanish noblewoman.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Fernando de la Cerda (1275-1322) and Juana Núñez de Lara, called "la Palomilla". On her father's side she was a granddaughter of Princess Blanche of France and therefore a great-granddaughter of King Louis 
2 CONC IX (St. Louis) and Marguerite of Provence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanca was the second wife of Juan Manuel, Duke of Penafiel (1282-1349), a member of the junior branch of the Castilian royal house. Their daughter Juana Manuel of Castile married the (illegitimate) Henry II of Castile and became 
2 CONC Queen consort of Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanca Fernanda de la Cerda was a direct matrilineal ancestor of Queen Victoria and many other European nobles.
