2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT John II de Montfort de Dreux, 2nd Earl of Richmond1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, , b. 1239, d. 18 November 1305
2 CONT
2 CONT      John II de Montfort de Dreux, 2nd Earl of Richmond was born in 1239.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 He was the son of Jean I de Dreux, Duc de Bretagne and Blanche de Navarre. He married Beatrice of England, daughter of Henry III, King of England and Eleanor of Provence, on 22 January 1260 at Abbey of St. Denis, Saint-Denis, Îl
2 CONC e-de-France, France.1 He died on 18 November 1305.
2 CONT
2 CONT      John II de Montfort de Dreux, 2nd Earl of Richmond gained the title of Duc de Bretagne in 1286.1 He gained the title of 2nd Earl of Richmond.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John II de Montfort de Dreux, 2nd Earl of Richmond and Beatrice of England
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Henry de Dreux2 d. 1284
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Arthur II de Montfort, Duc de Bretagne+2 b. 1262, d. 1312
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.John de Bretagne, 3rd Earl of Richmond2 b. c 1266, d. 17 Jan 1333/34
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Marie de Bretagne de Dreux+2 b. 1268
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.Pierre de Dreux, Comte de Léon2 b. c 1269, d. 1312
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.Blanche de Bretagne2 b. c 1270, d. 1327
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.Alice de Dreux2 b. 1274, d. c 1329
2 CONT
2 CONT John II, Duke of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT  This article does not cite any references or sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unsourced material may be challenged and removed. (October 2008) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Coat of Arms of Peter I, Duke of Brittany and his successors.John II (in Breton Yann II, in French Jean II de Dreux) (1239 – 18 November 1305) was Duke of Brittany and Earl of Richmond, from 1286 to his death. He was son of Duke J
2 CONC ean I and Blanche, princess of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 22 January 1260, John married Princess Beatrice of England, a daughter of King Henry III of England and Eleanor of Provence. They had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur II, Duke of Brittany 
2 CONT
2 CONT John de Bretagne, 1st Earl of Richmond 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie de Dreux, wife of Guy III of Châtillon (1268-1339) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre, Viscount de Leon (1269-1312) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche de Dreux, wife of Philip of Artois (1271-1327) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleonore, Abbess of Fontevrault (1274-1329) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was killed during the celebrations surrounding the coronation of Pope Clement V in 1305. John was leading the pope's horse through the crowd. So many spectators had piled atop the walls that one of them crumbled and collapsed r
2 CONC ight on top of the unfortunate duke.
