1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wikipedia: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_III%2C_Duke_of_Brabant John III, Duke of Brabant]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1311, as his father's gesture of rapprochement with France, he married '''Marie d'Evreux (d. 1335), the daughter of count Louis d'Évreux and Marguerite d'Artois'''. They had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna, Duchess of Brabant (1322–1406)
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Brabant (February 9, 1323 – 1368), married at Saint-Quentin on June 6, 1347 Louis II of Flanders
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Brabant (1325 – March 1, 1399), Lady of Turnhout, married at Tervuren on July 1, 1347 Reginald III of Guelders
2 CONT
2 CONT John (1327–1335/36)
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri (d. October 29, 1349)
2 CONT
2 CONT Godfrey (d. aft. February 3, 1352)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Marie of Évreux From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Marie d'Évreux Born	1303 Died	31 October 1335 Noble family	Capet Spouse(s)	John III, Duke of Brabant Father	Louis d'Évreux Mother	Margaret of Artois Marie d'Évreux (1303 – Octo
2 CONC ber 31, 1335) was the eldest child of Louis d'Évreux and his wife Margaret of Artois. She was a member of the House of Capet.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was Duchess of Brabant by her marriage to John III, Duke of Brabant. Her paternal grandmother being Marie of Brabant, she was a great-granddaughter of Henry III, Duke of Brabant and so, her husband's second cousin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie was the eldest of five children born to her parents. Marie's younger siblings included: Charles d'Évreux; Lord of Étampes, Philip III of Navarre; husband of Joan II of Navarre, and Jeanne d'Évreux; Queen of France by her mar
2 CONC riage to Charles IV of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage[edit] In 1311, Marie married John III, Duke of Brabant as his father's gesture of rapprochement with France. They had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna, Duchess of Brabant (1322–1406) Margaret of Brabant (February 9, 1323 – 1368), married at Saint-Quentin on June 6, 1347 Louis II of Flanders Marie of Brabant (1325 – March 1, 1399), Lady of Turnhout, married at Tervuren on 
2 CONC July 1, 1347 Reginald III of Guelders John (1327–1335/36) Henri (d. October 29, 1349) Godfrey (d. aft. February 3, 1352) Marie's daughter Joanna was the first woman to be Duchess of Brabant in her own right.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie died October 31, 1335, aged thirty-one or thirty-two.[1][2]
