2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II of Bar alternately Henri II of Bar (1190-1239) was a Count of Bar who reigned from 1214 to 1239. He died in Gaza while on Crusade.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Spouse and children
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1219 he married Philippa de Dreux (1192 † 1242), the daughter of Robert II of Dreux.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Bar (1220-1275), in 1240 she married Henry V of Luxembourg
2 CONT
2 CONT Thiébaut II of Bar (c. 1221-1291), Succeeded Henry II as Count of Bar
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri, 1249
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne (1225-1299), first married Frédéric de Blamont who died in 1255
2 CONT
2 CONT Renaud (died 1271)
2 CONT
2 CONT Erard (died 1335)
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle (died 1320)
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] See also
