2 CONT Died   1354    Burial   Church of Notre-Dame in Cambrai    Spouse   Guyotte of Lille    Issue   John I, Lord of Ligny    House   Luxembourg    Father   Waleran I of Luxembourg, Lord of Ligny    Mother   Joan of Beauvoir    Waleran
2 CONC  II of Luxembourg, Lord of Ligny (French: Waléran II de Luxembourg II; German: Walram II. von Ligny; died 1354), was a French nobleman and member of the House of Luxembourg . He was Lord of Beauvoir, Roussy  and Ligny. He was a so
2 CONC n of Waleran I  and his wife, Joan of Beauvoir.  Walram initially inherited the castles of Beauvoir and Roussy from his mother. After the death of his brother Henry II  in 1303, he also inherited his father's Lordship of Ligny.  H
2 CONC e died in 1354 and was buried in the church of Notre-Dame in Cambrai.  He was married to Guyotte (died 1338), the heiress of the Burgraviate of Lille. Together they had a son:  	John I  (died 1364). External links 	Page at genealo
2 CONC gie-mittelalter.de
