1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Voir [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_Ier_de_Clermont_de_Nesle '''Wikipedia...''']
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Guy I of Clermont (1286 – Kortrijk, July 11, 1302) was Lord of Breteuil and Offemont and a Marshal of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the youngest son of Simon II of Clermont and Adele of Montfort.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1296 he became Marshal of France, when his elder brother Raoul of Clermont was already Constable of France. Together with his brother, he fought in 1302 against the Flemish in the Battle of the Golden Spurs, and both were kille
2 CONC d.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Golden_Spurs
2 CONT
2 CONT Categories: Marshals of France 1286 births 1302 deaths French military personnel killed in action This page was last modified on 7 October 2011 at 19:51.
