1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margherita_di_Borbone-Clermont_(1438-1483)_
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Bourbon (5 February 1438 – 24 April 1483) was the daughter of Charles I, Duke of Bourbon (1401–1456) and Agnes of Burgundy (1407–1476).
2 CONT
2 CONT On 6 April 1472, she became the first wife of Philip II, Duke of Savoy (1443–1497).[1] Her children from this marriage were:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Louise (1476–1531), married Charles d'Orléans, Count of Angoulême, had children including:
2 CONT **Francis I of France[2] whose daughter Margaret of Valois married to Emanuele Filiberto of Savoy.[2]
2 CONT **Marguerite of Navarre (1492–1549); Queen consort of King Henry II of Navarre
2 CONT *Girolamo (1478)
2 CONT *Philibert II (1480–1504)
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 24 April 1483 at the Chateau de Pont d'Ain.
