1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VIII,_Duke_of_Savoy ''[45 languages]''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Amadeus VIII''' (4 September 1383 – 7 January 1451), nicknamed '''the Peaceful''', was Count of Savoy from 1391 to 1416 and Duke of Savoy from 1416 to 1440. He was the first to hold the ducal title, granted by Emperor [https://
2 CONC www.geni.com/people/Re-Sigismondo-di-Lussemburgo/6000000001500854063 Sigismund]. Known for his diplomatic temperament and administrative reforms, he strengthened the state's institutions and fostered internal peace.
2 CONT He also claimed the papacy from 1439 to 1449 as '''Antipope Felix V''',[a] in opposition to Popes [https://www.geni.com/people/Pope-Eugene-IV/6000000010293952225 Eugene IV] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Pope-Nicholas-V/60000000
2 CONC 22945004064 Nicholas V], becoming the last historical antipope recognised by a significant portion of the Catholic clergy.
2 CONT {{https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vigiles_du_roi_Charles_VII_17_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Vigiles_du_roi_Charles_VII_17_%28cropped%29.jpg|right|140px}}
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VIII,_Duke_of_Savoy#Count_and_duke  Count and duke]
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VIII,_Duke_of_Savoy#Pope_of_the_Council_of_Basel  Pope of the Council of Basel]
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VIII,_Duke_of_Savoy#Later_life Later life]
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VIII,_Duke_of_Savoy#Marriage_and_issue  Marriage and issue]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Amadeus VIII (Pope Felix V), Duke of Savoy1
2 CONT Last Edited	29 Sep 2009
2 CONT '''M, #19235, b. 4 September 1383, d. 7 January 1451'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	Amadeus VII 'the Red', Duke of Savoy b. 24 Feb 1360, d. 1 Nov 1391
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Bonna du Berry b. 1366, d. 30 Dec 1435
2 CONT Charts	14 Generation Pedigree of George III, King of Great Britain & Ireland (#1)
2 CONT 14 Generation Pedigree of George III, King of Great Britain & Ireland (#2)
2 CONT 14 Generation Pedigree of Friedrich Wilhelm III, King of Prussia
2 CONT '''Amadeus VIII (Pope Felix V), Duke of Savoy was born on 4 September 1383 at Chambery, Savoy. He married Mary of Burgundy''', daughter of Philip II 'the Bold', Duke of Burgundy and Marguerite de Dampierre, '''in May 1401. Amadeus
2 CONC  VIII (Pope Felix V), Duke of Savoy died on 7 January 1451 at Geneva, Switzerland, at age 67.'''
2 CONT '''Family	Mary of Burgundy''' b. Aug 1380, d. 2 Oct 1422
2 CONT '''Children'''	
2 CONT *Margareta of Savoy2 b. 13 May 1405, d. 1418
2 CONT *Anton of Savoy2 b. 1407, d. b 12 Dec 1407
2 CONT *Anton of Savoy2 b. 1408, d. a 10 Oct 1408
2 CONT *Maria of Savoy b. c 31 Jan 1411, d. Dec 1469
2 CONT *Amadeus of Savoy, Prince of Piedmont2 b. 26 Mar 1412, d. 17 Aug 1431
2 CONT *Louis I, Duke of Savoy+ b. 24 Feb 1413, d. 29 Jan 1465
2 CONT *Bona of Savoy2 b. Sep 1415, d. 25 Sep 1430
2 CONT *Philipp of Savoy, Graf von Genf2 b. 1417, d. 3 Mar 1444
2 CONT *Anton of Savoy2 b. c 1418
2 CONT *Anton of Savoy2 b. c 1420
2 CONT *Margaret of Savoy+3 b. 7 Aug 1420, d. 30 Sep 1479
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1. [S5914] Unknown author, Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles by Paget, Vol. II, p. 283.
2 CONT 2. [S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. II, Tafel 192.
2 CONT 3. [S2] Detlev Schwennicke, Europaische Stammtafeln, New Series, Vol. I/2, Tafel 256.
