2 CONT 2. W.A. Beelaerts van Blokland, ‘The Viscounts of Leiden before 1339’, De Nederlandsche Leeuw 39 (1921) 215-222.
2 CONT 3. C. Hoek, ‘The Lords of Matenesse’, De Nederlandsche Leeuw 82 (1965) 32-58.
2 CONT 4. A.D.A. Monna, ‘The Possessions of the Leiden Viscountship’, in: Idem and W.H. Lenselink, Studies on the Zeeland and Leiden Viscountships (Groningen 1976) 63-106.
2 CONT 5. J.A. Coldewey, The Lords of Kuyc 1096-1400 (Tilburg 1981). Book of Charters of Holland and Zeeland until 1299, J.G. Kruisheer ed., 2 (Assen 1986).
2 CONT 6. J.C. Kort, ‘Repertory of the Count's Fiefs in the Rhineland’, Ons Voorrijzen 42 (1987) 690-721.
2 CONT 7. C.J.C. Broer, ‘Wife, Partner, Fellow Sufferer. On Charters as Sources for Women's History’, in: M. Mostert et al. eds., Woman, Family and Power. Sources on Women in the Middle Ages (Hilversum 1990) 147-166.
2 CONT 8. A. Janse, Who was Willem van Oegstgeest (1201)? (Oegstgeest 2001).
2 CONT 9. F. Lugt, The Estate of Oestgeest. The Middle Ages in Oegstgeest, Poelgeest, Kerkwerve, Rijnsburg and Nieuw-Rhijngeest (Leiden 2009).
