2 CONT …..
2 CONT 4.         JAN van Kuyc (-after 25 Jan 1312).  Provost at Utrecht and Louvain: “Johannes dns de Cuyk” established jurisdictional limits in his lands, with the consent of “collateralis nostre...Juthe dne de Cuyk nec non filiorum no
2 CONC strorum Johannis Sancti Servatii Trajectensis et Lovaniensis ecclesiarum ppti. et Ottonis dni de Zeelehem militis, ac nepotis nostri Johannis de Cuyk”, by charter dated 20 Apr 1308[1335].  The testament of “Jutta de Nassau relicta
2 CONC  domini Johannis quondam domini de Kuyc bone memorie”, dated 25 Jan 1312, bequeathed property to “dominum de Kuyc meum nepotem”, sealed by “dominorum Johannis...prepositi et Ottonis militis de Kuyc meorum liberorum, Johannis domin
2 CONC i de Kuyc mei nepotis”[1336]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Internal Sourcing:
2 CONT [1335] Wap (1858), Oorkonden, p. 245. 
2 CONT [1336] Wap (1858), Oorkonden, p. 257. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Cawley, Charles. “DUTCH NOBILITY.” Fmg.ac, 2025, fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/DUTCH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc62491900.
