2 CONT 7.         AGNES van Kuyc (-1345, bur Heysterbach).  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not been identified.  Butkens records her parentage and marriage, the couple’s dates of death and their place of burial[1346]
2 CONC .  "Henricus dominus de Lewenberg et...Agnes collateralis et uxor eiusdem" sold “dominium nostrum et judicium...apud Aldenrode upper Heide” to “domino nostro domino Adolfo comite de Monte” by charter dated 19 May 1311[1347].  "Hei
2 CONC nrich here van Lewinberg ind Agnes unse...wif" confirmed allegiance to “grave Wilhelm van Gulge” by charter dated 21 Jan 1333[1348].  
