2 CONT Jan, graaf van Horne is our 6th cousin 15 times removed.
2 CONT Janet Milburn
2 CONT 8/3/23
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikepedia:
2 CONT Jan van Horne (1480-1540)
2 CONT John van Horne
2 CONT after 1480 - 1540
2 CONT 4th Earl of Horne
2 CONT Period	1531 - 1540
2 CONT Predecessor	Jacob III van Horne
2 CONT Successor	Philip of Montmorency
2 CONT Father	Jacob II van Horne
2 CONT Mother	Johanna van Gruuthuse
2 CONT Dynasty	House Horne
2 CONT Jan van Horne (after 1480? - December 10 , 1540 ) was the fourth Count of Horne from 1531 to 1540.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a son of Count Jacob II van Horne and Johanna van Brugge, a daughter of Lodewijk van Gruuthuse .
2 CONT
2 CONT As a younger son, he embarked on a church career, while his brother Jacob succeeded their father. Jan held the influential position of provost of the Chapter of Saint Lambert in Liège and appeared to be a candidate for the office 
2 CONC of prince-bishop , position already filled by his uncle Johan van Horne .
2 CONT
2 CONT When it turned out that his brother Jacob III would not produce an heir for the county of Horne from three successive marriages, and Jan had to take care of the succession, he left the clergy, with dispensation from 'Rome', and ma
2 CONC rried Anna van Egmont, daughter of Floris van Egmont . She had previously been married to Joseph of Montmorency , by whom she had four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his brother's death in Vercelli , he himself became Count of Horne, lord of Heusden , Altena and Weert . However, his marriage remained childless. With the permission of his feudal lord, the Prince-Bishop of Liège Cornelis v
2 CONC an Bergen , he bequeathed the County of Horne to his wife's eldest son, Philip of Montmorency , by will .
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestors 
