2 CONT http://translate.google.com/translate?hl=en&sl=nl&u=http://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_van_Marnix&ei=s0_PT4HbA8nl6gHD7aX7Cw&sa=X&oi=translate&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CGAQ7gEwAA&prev=/search%3Fq%3D%25E2%2580%25A2Jan%2Bde%2BMarnix%26h
2 CONC l%3Den%26biw%3D1600%26bih%3D805%26prmd%3Dimvns
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan van Marnix ( Brussels , between 14 February 1537 and 14 February 1538 - Oosterweel , 13 March 1567 ) was a southern Dutch nobleman , brother of Philip of Marnix . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan de (of) Marnix, lord of Toulouse , was a member of the ' Compromise ', in which the Calvinist -noble element represented. He designed the first petition and killed in the battle of Oosterweel , often seen as the first battle o
2 CONC f the Eighty Years' War
