1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gautier_III_d%27Enghien
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HAINAUT.htm#GauthierIVEnghiendied1345 <br/>
2 CONT GAUTHIER [III] d'Enghien, son of GAUTHIER [II] Seigneur d'Enghien & his wife Yolande de Flandre (5 Jun 1302-[16 Oct] 1345).  Matthieu records his date of birth (no source cited)[1410].  Seigneur d'Enghien.  “Yolens feme jadis a...
2 CONC Wautier Sign Dayngh” promised that, for so long as she held “le Mambour nie de le tre no...fil Wautier Sign Daungh”, she would hold “toutes les fortereches à le dite tre Dayngh” loyally by charter dated mid-Nov 1310[1411].  “...Wa
2 CONC tiers sire d’Enghien...Ernouls d’Enghien sires de Prayaus...” witnessed the charter dated 10 Mar 1315 (O.S.) under which “Florens Bertaus sires de Mallines” transferred all his rights over Mechelen to Guillaume Comte de Hainaut[14
2 CONC 12].  Matthieu records that Gauthier authorised the foundation of a chaplaincy by “Ysabiaus de Rotebrughe, veuve de Watiers dou Risoit”, who donated land at Haute-Croix and Castre, by charter dated 25 Apr 1345 (no source cited, bu
2 CONC t noting that “une copie de ces lettres existe aux archives de la cure d’Enghien”)[1413].  The primary source which confirms his date of death has not been identified (Matthieu does not record the date). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (contract Jan 1321) ISABELLE de Brienne, daughter of GAUTHIER [V] Comte de Brienne Duke of Athens & his wife Jeanne de Châtillon (-28 Dec 1360).  The Istoria of Marino Sanudo Torsello records that "[il figlio]…[del] conte 
2 CONC de Brenna" had one daughter who married "al signor d’Angloin" who the son "della figlia del conte di Fiandra"[1414].  She claimed to succeed her brother in 1356 as Contessa di Lecce, Contessa di Conversano.  Dame de Ramerupt. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gauthier [III] & his wife had thirteen children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT --------
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter of Enghien (June 5, 1322 – November 18, 1340)
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabeau of Enghien (d. December 28, 1357), Abbess of Flines
2 CONT
2 CONT Sohier of Enghien (d. March 21, 1364), Count of Brienne, titular Duke of Athens.
2 CONT
2 CONT John of Enghien, (d. 1380), Count of Lecce and Lord of Castro
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite of Enghien, married Pierre de Préaux
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis of Enghien (d. March 17, 1394), Lord (later Count) of Conversano, later Count of Brienne and titular Duke of Athens. Married Giovanna of Sanseverino, by whom he had four daughters, including his heiress, Marguerite, who in h
2 CONC er own turn married John of Luxembourg, Sire of Beauvois. Mary, Queen of Scots and Queen consort Elizabeth Woodville were notable descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques of Enghien, a canon in Liège
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy of Enghien,(d. 1377), Lord of Argos and Nauplia
2 CONT
2 CONT Engelbert I of Enghien (c. 1330–February 20, 1403), Lord of Ramerupt, La Follie, and Seneffe
2 CONT
2 CONT Françoise of Enghien, married Peter, Count of Montebello
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne of Enghien, a nun at Flines
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Relationship to Lady Jane Grey:'''
2 CONT
