0 @N6000000002187746299@ NOTE John II, Count of Hainaut
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT John II of Avesnes (1247 – August 22, 1304) was count of Hainaut from 1278 to his death, succeeding his father, John I. He became Count of Holland in 1299 with the death of John I, Count of Holland, through his mother Adelaide of 
1 CONC Holland, heiress and regent of this county. His descendants maintained this personal union between the counties.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Family and children
1 CONT In 1270, John married Philippine of Luxemburg, daughter of Count Henry II of Luxemburg and Marguerite of Bar. They children were:
1 CONT
1 CONT John, senior de Beaumont, Count of Ostervant (d. [[11 July 1302). 
1 CONT Henry, a canon in Cambrai, (d. 1303). 
1 CONT Simon. 
1 CONT William III, Count of Hainaut. 
1 CONT Jean,senior de Beaumont, (1288 – 11 March 1356). He was married Marguerite, Countess de Soissons. 
1 CONT Margaret, (d. 18 October 1342), married Robert II of Artois. 
1 CONT Alix, (d. 26 October 1317), married 1290 Roger Bigod, 5th Earl of Norfolk. 
1 CONT Isabelle, (d. 1305); married Raoul de Clermont, senior de Nesle. 
1 CONT Jeanne, a nun at Fontenelles. 
1 CONT Marie (1280–1354),married Louis I, Duke of Bourbon. 
1 CONT Matilda, Abbess of Nivelles. 
1 CONT   This biography of a European noble is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it. 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT See also
1 CONT Counts of Hainaut family tree 
1 CONT Counts of Holland family tree 
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT John I Count of Hainaut Succeeded by:
1 CONT William III 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT John I Count of Holland 
0 @N6000000003051245081@ NOTE [Wikipedia, "John II, Count of Holland", retrieved 22 Dec 07]
1 CONT John II of Avesnes (1247-August 22, 1304) was the oldest son of John I of Avesnes and Adelaide of Holland.
1 CONT
1 CONT History
1 CONT John II was Count of Hainaut from 1280 to his death, succeeding his grandmother, Margaret II. John continued the war between the House of Dampierre and the House of Avesnes against count Guy of Flanders for imperial Flanders.
1 CONT
1 CONT He became Count of Holland in 1299 with the death of John I, Count of Holland, through his mother Adelaide of Holland, heiress and regent of this county. His descendants maintained this personal union between the counties.
1 CONT
1 CONT His nephew, Count Floris V, was fighting against Flanders for Zeeland. He sought help of France against Flanders. The French defeated the Flemish in 1300 and 1301. The rebels in Zeeland were defeated as well. John's brother, Guy o
1 CONC f Avesnes, became Bishop of Utrecht. So all his main enemies were gone.
1 CONT
1 CONT The tide changed dramatically after a Flemish uprising and the defeat of the French army at the Battle of the Golden Spurs in 1302. Flemish patriots attacked Hainaut and Zeeland supported by the dissatisfied population there. Guy 
1 CONC of Namur defeated John's son, William, in a battle on the island of Duiveland. Bishop Guy of Utrecht was taken prisoner. Guy of Namur and Duke John II of Brabant conquered most of Utrecht, Holland, and Zeeland. Guy of Namur was fi
1 CONC nally defeated in 1304 by the fleet of Holland and France at the naval Battle of Zierikzee. John II regained most of his authority when he died in the same year.
1 CONT
1 CONT Family
1 CONT In 1270, John married Philippine of Luxemburg, daughter of Count Henry II of Luxemburg and Marguerite of Bar. Their children were:
1 CONT - John, senior de Beaumont, Count of Ostervant (d. 11 July 1302).
1 CONT - Henry, a canon in Cambrai, (d. 1303).
1 CONT - Simon.
1 CONT - William I, Count of Hainaut.
1 CONT - Jean, senior de Beaumont, (1288 ? 11 March 1356). He was married to Marguerite, Countess de Soissons.
1 CONT - Margaret, (d. 18 October 1342), married Robert II of Artois.
1 CONT - Alix, (d. 26 October 1317), married 1290 Roger Bigod, 5th Earl of Norfolk.
1 CONT - Isabelle, (d. 1305), married Raoul de Clermont, senior de Nesle.
1 CONT - Jeanne, a nun at Fontenelles.
1 CONT - Marie (1280?1354), married Louis I, Duke of Bourbon.
1 CONT - Matilda, Abbess of Nivelles.
1 CONT - Willem de Cuser (b. 1290)
