0 @N6000000004533185605@ NOTE From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Isabella of Aragon (1247-January 28, 1271), infanta of Aragon, was, bymarriage, queen of France from 1270 to 1271.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was the daugther of James the Conqueror, king of Aragon, Valencia,and Majorca, and his second wife Yolande of Hungary, daughter ofAndrew II of Hungary. On May 28, 1262, she married the future PhilipIII of France, son of king L
1 CONC ouis IX and Marguerite Berenger ofProvence, in Clermont.
1 CONT
1 CONT Their children were:
1 CONT
1 CONT Louis (1264-1276)
1 CONT Philip IV "the Fair" (1268-1314), king of France
1 CONT Robert (1269-c. 1276)
1 CONT Charles of Valois (1270-1325)
1 CONT She accompanied her husband on the Eighth Crusade against Tunis, butdied after falling from her horse on the way home, in Cosenza,Calabria, still pregnant with her fifth child. She was buried in SaintDenis Basilica. Her tomb, like
1 CONC  many others, was desecrated during theFrench Revolution in 1793.
