0 @N6000000002188307854@ NOTE Blanche d'Évreux
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Blanche d'Évreux (1331 – 1398) was the Queen consort of Philip VI of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was born a princess of Navarre, daughter of the queen regnant Joan II of Navarre and Philip d'Évreux.
1 CONT
1 CONT Blanche and King Philip VI married on January 11, 1350. She was his second wife, after Joan who died of the plague. They had one daughter: Jeanne (1351–1371), who was intended to marry John I of Aragon, but who died upon the journ
1 CONC ey.
1 CONT
1 CONT Blanche was interested in alchemy and had laboratories in some of her castles. She sponsored Nicolas Flamel.
1 CONT
1 CONT A 20th century hoax alleged her to have been the 7th Grand Master of the Priory of Sion.
1 CONT
