0 @N6000000002187746405@ NOTE John I, Count of Hainaut
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT John I of Avesnes (May 1, 1218 – December 24, 1257) was count of Hainaut from 1246 to his death. John was son of Countess Margaret II of Flanders and Hainaut as Margaret I, by her first husband, Count Bouchard IV of Avesnes. He in
1 CONC herited Hainaut, during Margaret's lifetime, while his half brother Guy of Dampierre became Count of Flanders.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Family and children
1 CONT He married Adelaide of Holland in 1246 and had the following issue:
1 CONT
1 CONT John II, Count of Hainaut and Holland (1247-1304) 
1 CONT Joanna, abbess of Flines (died 1304) 
1 CONT Bouchard, Bishop of Metz (1251-1296) 
1 CONT Guy, Bishop of Utrecht (1253-1317) 
1 CONT William, Bishop of Cambrai (1254-1296) 
1 CONT Floris, stadholder of Zeeland and Prince of Achaea 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT See also
1 CONT Counts of Hainaut family tree 
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Margaret I Count of Hainaut Succeeded by:
1 CONT John II 
