0 @N6000000002248207820@ NOTE Between 1258 and 1263, Adelaide was regent of Holland in the name of her nephew Floris V.  She died in 1284, but in 1299, with the death of Floris; son John I, it was her own son John II who inherited Holland through her.
0 @N6000000002187746416@ NOTE Adelaide of Holland
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Adelaide of Holland or Aleide (Aleidis) van Holland (circa 1222 – 1284) was a daughter of Floris IV, Count of Holland and sister of William II, Count of Holland and King of Germany. On October 9, 1246, Adelaide married John I of A
1 CONC vesnes, Count of Hainaut and had the following issue:[1]
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. John II, Count of Hainaut and Holland (1237-1304)
1 CONT    2. Joanna, abbess of Flines (died 1304)
1 CONT    3. Bouchard, Bishop of Metz (1251-1296)
1 CONT    4. Guy, Bishop of Utrecht (1253-1317)
1 CONT    5. William, Bishop of Cambrai (1254-1296)
1 CONT    6. Floris, stadholder of Zeeland and Prince of Achaea (1255-1297)
1 CONT
1 CONT Between 1258 and 1263, Adelaide was regent of Holland in the name of her nephew Floris V. She died in 1284, but in 1299, with the death of Floris' son John I, it was her own son John II who inherited Holland through her.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] See also
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Counts of Hainaut family tree
1 CONT     * Counts of Holland family tree
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. ^ Ancestors of Paul Bailey MCBRIDE. Paul B. McBride's Genealogy. Retrieved on 2006-11-11.
