0 @N6000000000437690750@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Duc Name Suffix:<NSFX> I
0 @N6000000002187582944@ NOTE Peter I, Duke of Bourbon
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Peter I of Bourbon (1311 – September 19, 1356, Poitiers) was the second Duke of Bourbon, from 1342 to his death.
1 CONT
1 CONT Peter was son of Louis I of Bourbon, whom he also succeeded as Grand Chamberlain of France, and Mary of Hainaut.
1 CONT
1 CONT Duke Peter is reported to have been mentally somewhat instable, a trait of nervous breakdowns presumably hereditary that showed clearly for example in his daughter Jeanne de Bourbon, the queen, and in her son, king Charles VI of F
1 CONC rance, as well as in Peter's only surviving son, Duke Louis II.
1 CONT
1 CONT On 25 January 1326 he married Isabella of Valois, daughter of Charles, Count of Valois and his third wife Mahaut of Chatillon. Peter and Isabella had only one son, Louis, and seven daughters. These were:
1 CONT
1 CONT Jeanne (1338–1378), married King Charles V of France 
1 CONT Blanche (1339–1361, Medina-Sidonia), married King Pedro of Castile in 1353 in Valladolid, poisoned by her husband 
1 CONT Bonne (1341 – January 19, 1402, Château de Mâcon), married Amadeus VI, Count of Savoy in 1355 in Paris 
1 CONT Catherine (1342–1427, Paris), married John VI, Count of Harcourt 
1 CONT Margaret (1344–1416), married Arnaud Amanieu, Viscount of Tartas 
1 CONT Isabelle (b. 1345) 
1 CONT Mary (1347–1401, Poissy), Prioress of Poissy 
1 CONT Peter died in the Battle of Poitiers.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT Foundation for Medieval Genealogy Accessed November 17, 2007 
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Louis I Duke of Bourbon
1 CONT Count of Clermont-en-Beauvaisis
1 CONT 1342–1356 Succeeded by
1 CONT Louis II 
1 CONT Count of La Marche
1 CONT 1342–1356 Succeeded by
1 CONT James I 
