0 @N6000000002187840112@ NOTE John, Duke of Berry
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT John of Valois, the Magnificent, (November 30, 1340 – March 15, 1416) was Duke of Berry and Auvergne and Count of Poitiers and Montpensier. He was the third son of King John II of France and Bonne of Luxemburg; amongst his sibling
1 CONC s were Charles V, King of France, Louis I, King of Naples and Philip II, Duke of Burgundy.
1 CONT
1 CONT In the middle of the Hundred Years' War and serious internal conflicts, John was a consensual figure in France. He acted several times as a peace maker between French factions and is notable by his attempts of peace between his ne
1 CONC phews Louis of Valois, Duke of Orléans and John, Duke of Burgundy.
1 CONT
1 CONT French Monarchy
1 CONT Capetian Dynasty
1 CONT (Valois branch)  
1 CONT
1 CONT Philip VI 
1 CONT Children 
1 CONT    John II 
1 CONT John II 
1 CONT Children 
1 CONT    Charles V 
1 CONT    Louis I of Anjou 
1 CONT    John, Duke of Berry 
1 CONT    Philip II, Duke of Burgundy 
1 CONT Charles V 
1 CONT Children 
1 CONT    Charles VI 
1 CONT    Louis, Duke of Orléans 
1 CONT Charles VI 
1 CONT Children 
1 CONT    Isabella of Valois 
1 CONT    Catherine of Valois 
1 CONT    Charles VII 
1 CONT Charles VII 
1 CONT Children 
1 CONT    Louis XI 
1 CONT Louis XI 
1 CONT Children 
1 CONT    Charles VIII 
1 CONT Charles VIII 
1 CONT
1 CONT John of Berry was a notable patron who among other works commissioned the most famous Book of Hours, the Très Riches Heures. His spending on his art collection severely taxed his estates, and he was deeply in debt when he died in 
1 CONC 1416.
1 CONT
1 CONT John of Berry had the following issue by his first wife, Joanna of Armagnac (1346–1387):
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles of Berry, Count of Montpensier (1362–1382) 
1 CONT John of Berry, Count of Montpensier (1363–1402), married princess Catherine of France 
1 CONT Louis of Berry (1364–1383) 
1 CONT Bonne of Berry (1365–1435), married Amadeus VII of Savoy and Bernard VII, Count of Armagnac 
1 CONT Marie of Berry, Duchess of Auvergne (1367–1434), married: 1) Louis III of Châtillon, 2) Philip of Artois, Count of Eu; 3) John I, Duke of Bourbon 
