0 @N6000000002188651594@ NOTE Raoul II of Lusignan
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Raoul II of Lusignan or Raoul II de Lusignan (c. 1200 – c. September 1, 1246/September, 1250, buried at the Abbey of Foucarmont), was the son of Raoul I of Lusignan and second wife Alix d'Eu. He became Seigneur d'Issoudun, Count o
1 CONC f Eu and of Guines on May 1, 1219.
1 CONT
1 CONT Married firstly in 1222 to Jeanne de Bourgogne (1200 – 1223, buried at the Abbaye de Foncarmont), daughter of Eudes III of Burgundy and second wife Alix de Vergy, and had issue, one only daughter, married secondly after 1223 Yolan
1 CONC de de Dreux (1196 – October 16, 1239), without issue, and married thirdly after 1239 Philippe de Dammartin (1225-1230 – April 14, 1278/1281, buried at the Abbey of 's-Gravendaal), daughter of Simon de Dammartin, Comte d’Aumale, de
1 CONC  Ponthieu et de Montreuil, and wife Marie de Ponthieu, without issue. His only daughter was:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Marie de Lusignan
