0 @N6000000002322305156@ NOTE As great-grandson of Stephen V, Charles claimed the throne of Hungary,
1 CONT succeeding Andrew III King of Hungary (last of the direct line of the Arpad
1 CONT dynasty). His claim was disputed, but, eventually, he was finally recognized
1 CONT as king and received the Crown of St. Stephen at Szekesfehervar on August 27,
1 CONT 1310. A courtly, pius king, he restored his kingdom to the status of a great
1 CONT power and enriched and civilized it. His foreign policy was aimed at family
1 CONT aggrandizement, but it also greatly benefited Hungary
0 @N6000000002176658324@ NOTE As great-grandson of Stephen V, Charles claimed the throne of Hungary,
1 CONT succeeding Andrew III King of Hungary (last of the direct line of the Arpad
1 CONT dynasty). His claim was disputed, but, eventually, he was finally recognized
1 CONT as king and received the Crown of St. Stephen at Szekesfehervar on August 27,
