0 @N6000000002188383193@ NOTE Otto V, Duke of Bavaria
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Otto V, Duke of Bavaria (1346 – November 15, 1379), was duke of Bavaria and margrave-elector of Brandenburg. Otto was the fourth son of Louis IV, Holy Roman Emperor with his second wife Margaret II of Avesnes, countess of Hainaut 
1 CONC and Holland.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Biography
1 CONT
1 CONT Jointly duke of Bavaria with his five brothers in 1347, he and his brothers Louis V and Louis VI became joint dukes of Upper Bavaria after the partition of Bavaria in 1349. In 1351, he and Louis VI gave up their rights in Bavaria 
1 CONC to Louis V in return for the Margraviate of Brandenburg. In 1356 Louis VI and Otto were invested with the electoral dignity.
1 CONT
1 CONT Otto, still a minor, grew up in his mother's lands in the Netherlands under tutelage of his brother Louis V. In 1360 Otto came to age. With the death of Louis VI in 1365 Otto became sole Margrave-Elector of Brandenburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT On March 19, 1366, Otto married Katharine of Bohemia (1342 – 86), daughter of Charles IV, Holy Roman Emperor and widow of Rudolf IV, Duke of Austria, since the childless dukes Louis VI and Otto had already promised Charles the suc
1 CONC cession in Brandenburg in 1364. This contract was revenge for a conflict with their brother Stephen II on Bavarian succession after the death of Meinhard III of Gorizia-Tyrol, son of Louis V.
1 CONT
1 CONT However Charles invaded Brandenburg in 1371 since Otto neglected his government. Two years later Otto officially resigned against a huge financial compensation and retired in Bavaria. This was the end of the Wittelsbach rule in Br
1 CONC andenburg. Otto kept the electoral dignity and was accepted as nominal co-regent by Stephen II. Otto then spent his time in Wolfstein castle in Landshut with amusements.
1 CONT
