1 CONT 1.   Philippa Plantagenet, mar John I, King of Portugal and had issue.
1 CONT 2.   Elizabeth Plantagenet, mar John Holland, 1st Duke of Exeter and had issue.
1 CONT 3.   Henry IV, born 1366, succeeded 13th Oct 1399 (House of Lancaster).
1 CONT
1 CONT through his wife inherited Kenilworth Castle, Warwickshire (later held by Robert Dudley),
1 CONT he was the effective ruler late Edward III - early Richard II,
1 CONT appears in Richard II by Shakespeare,
1 CONT the TV movie Richard II (1978) has John Gielgud as John of Gaunt,
1 CONT patron of John Wycliffe, the "Morning Star of the Reformation", who produced the first English translation of the Bible 1382,
1 CONT mar 3rdly, 1396, to his long-time mistress Catherine Roet [born 1350], by whom he had already had illegitimate issue,
1 CONT his children by Catherine Roet were legitimated by statute 1397 "for all purposes save succession to the crown" (i.e. this line is not in the Royal line of succession, but of course we have other Royal Descents),
1 CONT he died 3rd Feb 1399, age 58 yrs, bur St.Paul's Cathedral, London,
1 CONT see biography,
1 CONT never king himself, but within months of his death his son became king,
