0 @N6000000002187840181@ NOTE Robert II, Duke of Burgundy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert II of Burgundy (1248 – March 21, 1306) was duke of Burgundy between 1271 and 1306. Robert was the third son of duke Hugh IV and Yolande of Dreux. Robert married princess Agnes of France, youngest daughter of king Louis IX i
1 CONC n 1279 and had the following issue:
1 CONT
1 CONT Hugh V, Duke of Burgundy (1282–1315) 
1 CONT Blanche (1288–1348), married Edward of Savoy 
1 CONT Marguerite (1290- 1315), married king Louis X of France 
1 CONT Joan (Jeanne) (ca.1290–1348), married count of Maine and Valois, king Philip VI of France 
1 CONT Eudes IV, Duke of Burgundy (1295–1350) 
1 CONT Louis, King of Thessalonica (1297–1316), married Matilda of Hainaut 
1 CONT Mary (1298–1336) married Edward I of Bar 
1 CONT Robert, count of Tonnerre (1302–1334), married Joanna, heiress of Tonnerre 
1 CONT Robert ended the practice of giving away parts of the Burgundian estate to younger sons and as dowries to the daughters. From then on, the whole duchy, however already diminished by earlier dowries, passed unfragmented to the elde
1 CONC st son.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] See also
1 CONT Dukes of Burgundy family tree 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] External links
