0 @N6000000002187840133@ NOTE Jeanne de Valois, Queen of Navarre
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Jeanne de Valois, or Joan of France (June 24, 1343, Chateauneuf-en-Loire – November 3, 1373, Évreux), was the daughter of John II of France (called The Good), and his first wife, Bonne of Luxembourg. She married Charles II of Nava
1 CONC rre (called The Bad), and became Queen-consort of Navarre.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was married to Charles the Bad in February 1352, at Chateau du Vivier, close to Fontenay-Trésigny in Brie. He was her second cousin.
1 CONT
1 CONT She had the following children with Charles:
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Marie (1360, Puente la Reina – aft. 1400), married in Tudela on January 20, 1393 Alfonso d'Aragona, Duke of Gandia (d. 1412)
1 CONT    2. Charles III of Navarre (1361–1425)
1 CONT    3. Bonne (1364 – aft. 1389)
1 CONT    4. Peter of Évreux, Count of Mortain (c. March 31, 1366, Évreux – c. July 29, 1412, Bourges), married in Alençon on April 21, 1411 Catherine (1380–1462), daughter of Peter II of Alençon
1 CONT    5. Philip (b. 1368), d. young
1 CONT    6. Joanna of Navarre (1370–1437), married first John V, Duke of Brittany, married second Henry IV of England
1 CONT    7. Blanca (1372–1385, Olite)
1 CONT
