0 @N6000000002188376164@ NOTE Marie of Anjou
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Marie of Anjou (October 14, 1404–1463) was the daughter of Louis II of Anjou, King of Naples, titular King of Sicily, and Yolande of Aragon, Queen of Aragon, herself daughter of John I of Aragon.
1 CONT
1 CONT She married King Charles VII in 1422 at Bourges, and became queen consort of France. However, her husband's affection was primarily directed towards his mistress, Agnès Sorel.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marie was the mother of twelve children
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Louis XI, King of France (1423-1483)
1 CONT     * John of France (1424-1425)
1 CONT     * Radegonde de France (1428-1444)
1 CONT     * Catherine (1428-1446), married Charles de Charolais, future Charles le Téméraire, Duke of Burgundy, in 1440
1 CONT     * Jacques de France (1432-1437)
1 CONT     * Yolande de France (1434-1478), married the future Amadeus IX, Duke of Savoy in 1452. Upon his death in 1472, she became regent of Savoy.
1 CONT     * Joan (1435-1482), married the future John II, Duke of Bourbon in 1452
1 CONT     * Margaret of France (1437-1438)
1 CONT     * Mary of France (7 September 1438 - 14 February 1439)
1 CONT     * Jeanne (7 September 1438 - 26 December 1446)
1 CONT     * Magdalena of Valois (1443-1486), married Gaston de Foix,
1 CONT     * Charles, Duc de Berry (1446-1472)
1 CONT
