0 @N6000000002188309498@ NOTE Isabella, Duchess of Lorraine
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Isabella (1400 – February 28, 1453) was Duchess of Lorraine from 1431 to her death.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was a daughter of Charles II, Duke of Lorraine and Margaret of the Palatinate. Her maternal grandparents were Rupert of Germany and Elisabeth of Nuremberg, daughter of Burgrave Frederick V of Nuremberg and Elisabeth of Meissen
1 CONC .
1 CONT
1 CONT Isabella inherited the duchy from her father and ruled with her husband, Duke René of Anjou, also Duke of Bar and King of Naples. During his absence, she acted as regent for his domains. She led an army to rescue her husband from 
1 CONC Philip III, Duke of Burgundy.
1 CONT
1 CONT They had the following issue:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * John II of Anjou and King of Naples (1425-1470)
1 CONT     * Yolande of Anjou (1428-1483), married Frederick of Lorraine, count of Vaudemont; mother of duke René II of Lorraine
1 CONT     * Margaret of Anjou (1429-1482), married king Henry VI of England
1 CONT     * plus seven others who died in childhood
1 CONT
1 CONT See also: Dukes of Lorraine family tree
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Charles II Duchess of Lorraine
1 CONT with René I
1 CONT 1431-1453 Succeeded by
1 CONT John II
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT James II, Count of La Marche Queen Consort of Naples
1 CONT 1435–1442 Succeeded by
1 CONT Maria of Castile
