0 @N6000000002187845526@ NOTE Mahaut, Countess of Artois
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Mahaut of Artois (1268 – October 27, 1329, Paris), also known as Mathilda, was the daughter of Robert II, Count of Artois and Amicie de Courtenay.
1 CONT
1 CONT She married Otto IV, Count of Burgundy, to whom she bore three children, including two girls who married kings of France, Blanche and Jeanne. Because of the premature death of her brother Philip in 1298, she inherited the County o
1 CONC f Artois at her father's death in 1302, rather than her nephew Robert (her inheritance being based upon proximity of blood). Although he repeatedly challenged the decision, her rights to the County were consistently upheld. At her
1 CONC  death, the county was inherited by her daughter Jeanne II, Countess Palatine of Burgundy (d 1330), who was married to Philip V of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT She is portrayed by Jeanne Moreau in the 2005 French miniseries "Les Rois Maudits".
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Robert II Countess of Artois
1 CONT 1302–1329 Succeeded by
1 CONT Jeanne
